.\" sliver-stylesheet(5). The engine is crates/sliver-render/src/style.
.TH SLIVER\-STYLESHEET 5 2026-11-06 "sliver 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
sliver\-stylesheet \- Touch Bar stylesheet (style.css)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sliver/style.css
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Touch Bar is styled with a CSS stylesheet, like waybar's
.BR style.css .
The file sits next to the configuration
.RB ( sliver\-config (5)),
or wherever its
.B stylesheet
key points.
It is loaded on top of the built\-in theme chosen by the configuration's
.B theme
key (default
.BR sliver ).
.B style\-dark.css
and
.B style\-light.css
are used instead when present, following the desktop's color scheme.
Changes apply when the file is saved, imports included.
.PP
To see a stylesheet without the bar,
.B sliverctl render \-o
.I out.png
draws the bar as it is, and
.B sliver\-agent \-\-render
.I prefix
writes the base and Fn layers.
.SH ERRORS
Nothing in a stylesheet can blank the bar.
Each problem is reported as
.IB file : line : col : " message"\fR,
and only the offending declaration, selector or rule is dropped.
The built\-in safe layer of
.BR sliverd (8)
never uses your stylesheet.
.SH TREE
.EX
bar      classes: layer\-<name>, layout\-<name>, <bar name>, locked, dimmed
+\- zone   .zone\-<name> (.zone\-esc, .zone\-main, .zone\-controls by default),
   |       plus the zone's configured class
   +\- module  #<type>, .module, .<instance>, state classes, script and config classes
      +\- trough       sliders only
         +\- highlight   the filled part, up to the value
         +\- slider      the knob (drawn only when it has a min\-width)
.EE
.PP
Module ids are the type with
.B /
replaced by
.BR \- :
.BR #clock ,
.BR #battery ,
.BR #custom\-vpn ,
.BR #key\-f1 ,
.BR #group\-control\-strip .
.BI # id
only ever matches modules.
An instance becomes a class
.RB ( battery#bat2
is
.BR #battery.bat2 ).
.PP
State classes come from
.B states
.RB ( .warning ,
.BR .critical ),
the module's status
.RB ( .charging ,
.BR .muted ,
.BR .playing ,
\&...),
.B .on
(toggles that are on), a script's JSON
.BR class ,
the configured
.BR class ,
.B .error
(a failed script) and
.B .drawer\-child
(a drawer's hidden members).
Each module type's own classes are listed in
.BR sliver\-config (5).
Items published by apps also get
.BR .dbus ,
.B .app
or
.BR .status ,
their type
.RB ( .button ,
.BR .toggle ,
.BR .slider ,
\&...), their own classes, and
.B .focused\-app
while their app is focused.
A modal app context sets
.BR bar.modal ,
.B zone.zone\-modal
and
.B #modal\-close
on its close button.
.SH SELECTORS
.BR * ,
.BR bar ,
.BR zone ,
.BR module ,
the parts above,
.BI # id\fR,
.BI . class\fR,
.B :active
(pressed),
.B :checked
(a toggle that is on, or the selected segment; the built\-in themes treat
.B .on
the same),
.BR :disabled ,
.BR :first\-child ,
.BR :last\-child ,
.BR :not( \fIsimple\fP ) ,
descendant
.RB ( "a b" )
and child
.RB ( "a > b" )
combinators, and comma lists.
.B :hover
and
.B :focus
are accepted but never match on a touch strip.
Sibling combinators
.RB ( + ,
.BR ~ )
aren't supported.
Precedence is standard CSS:
.BR !important ,
then specificity, then later rules.
.SH PROPERTIES
.TP
.B color
Labels and symbolic icons.
Inherited.
.TP
.BR background ", " background\-color
Plain colors only; gradients and images aren't supported.
.TP
.B border
.RI [ width ]
.RB [ solid ]
.RI [ color ],
or
.BR none .
.TP
.BR border\-width ", " border\-color ", " border\-style
.B border\-color
defaults to
.BR color .
.B border\-style
is
.B solid
or
.B none
.RB ( hidden ).
.TP
.B border\-radius
A length.
Pictures are clipped to it.
.TP
.BR padding ", " padding\-top ", " padding\-right ", " padding\-bottom ", " padding\-left
1\(en4 lengths, inside the box.
Auto widths include it.
.TP
.BR margin ", " margin\-top ", " margin\-right ", " margin\-bottom ", " margin\-left
1\(en4 lengths, outside the box: it eats into the module's slot.
.TP
.B font\-family
A list; the first installed family wins.
.B sans\-serif
and unknown families mean the embedded Noto Sans.
Inherited.
.TP
.B font\-size
Labels shrink (down to half size) to fit, then are ellipsized.
Inherited.
.TP
.B font\-weight
.BR normal ,
.BR bold ,
or 100\(en900.
Inherited.
.TP
.BR \-sliver\-icon\-size " (" \-gtk\-icon\-size )
A length.
Inherited.
.TP
.B \-sliver\-icon\-fit
.B canvas
(default) or
.BR content .
.B content
sizes an icon by its visible artwork instead of its canvas, so icons whose files have different
transparent margins (app icons especially) come out the same size.
Inherited.
.TP
.B opacity
0\(en1 or a percentage.
It multiplies down the tree.
.TP
.B min\-width
On modules, the floor for
.B auto
widths.
On
.BR trough ,
its natural length.
On
.BR slider ,
the knob's width.
.TP
.B min\-height
On
.BR trough ,
its thickness (default 6 pixels).
On
.BR slider ,
the knob's height.
.TP
.BR gap " (" column\-gap )
Between zones (on
.BR bar ),
between modules (on
.BR zone ),
and between icon and label (on
.BR module ).
.TP
.B transition
.BR none ,
or a comma list of
.RI [ property ]
.I time
.RI [ timing ]
.RI [ delay ].
It animates
.BR color ,
.B background\-color
.RB ( background ),
.B border\-color
and
.B opacity
when a module's style changes (pressed, state classes,
.BR :checked ,
\&...).
.B width
(alias
.BR min\-width )
animates the box itself: when the layout resizes or moves a module or zone (a collapsed slider
opening, neighbours making room) it glides there, while touch regions are final at once.
.B all
means the four paint properties, not
.BR width ,
so a pasted
.B transition: all 0.3s
doesn't animate layout on every clock tick.
Timing functions:
.BR linear ,
.BR ease ,
.BR ease\-in ,
.BR ease\-out ,
.BR ease\-in\-out ,
.BR cubic\-bezier( \fIa\fP , \fIb\fP , \fIc\fP , \fId\fP ) .
Other properties
.RB ( transform ,
.BR height ,
\&...) are accepted and not animated.
.TP
.B \-sliver\-layer\-transition
On
.BR bar :
how the bar changes layer.
.BR none ,
or
.B slide
or
.B fade
with a
.I time
and an optional
.IR timing .
.B slide
pushes the old layer out: the new one comes from the right when you go into a layer (media, a
group) and from the left when you come back.
.B fade
cross\-fades.
When only the layout changes (an app's layout, a rule), it always fades.
A touch ends it at once, and touch regions are final from the start.
.PP
Animations are drawn at up to 60 frames a second, the panel's refresh, and only while something
moves; an idle bar costs nothing.
A change that covers the whole bar flushes at about 30 frames a second.
The pressed overlay that
.B sliverd
draws never animates.
The desktop's reduce\-motion setting turns every transition off, followed live: GNOME's
Animations switch
.RB ( org.gnome.desktop.interface
.BR enable\-animations ,
read through the settings portal) or KDE's animation speed set to instant
.RB ( AnimationDurationFactor=0
in
.BR kdeglobals ).
.PP
Lengths are
.BR px ,
.BR pt ,
.B em
(relative to the element's font size) or bare numbers (pixels).
.BR inherit ,
.B initial
and
.B unset
work everywhere.
Colors are anything CSS accepts
.RB ( #rgb[a] ,
.BR #rrggbb[aa] ,
.BR rgb() ,
.BR rgba() ,
.BR hsl() ,
names,
.BR transparent ,
.BR currentColor ),
plus GTK's
.BI @ name\fR,
.BI alpha( c ", " a )\fR,
.BI shade( c ", " k )\fR,
.BI mix( a ", " b ", " t )\fR,
.BI lighter( c )
and
.BI darker( c )\fR.
Unsupported properties are reported and skipped.
.SH PICTURES, GRAPHS AND SPECTRA
Pictures
.RB ( image
modules and items) fill the module's content box (inside
.BR padding )
at their aspect ratio and are clipped to its
.BR border\-radius .
.PP
A
.B graph
draws its line in
.B color
over an area filled with the same color at a quarter of its alpha, inside the content box with 15%
of its height free above and below.
.B width
or
.B min\-width
make it wider than its natural 60 pixels.
.SH AT\-RULES
.TP
.BI "@define\-color " "name value" ;
Must come before use.
.TP
.BI "@import \(dq" path "\(dq;"
Relative to the importing file.
.B @import \(dqsliver:classic\(dq;
imports a built\-in theme.
Imports nest up to 8 levels deep.
.PP
Other at\-rules
.RB ( @media ,
.BR @keyframes ,
\&...) are reported and skipped.
.SH THEMES
.TP
.B sliver
The default: the macOS Touch Bar look.
Toggles that are on and slider fills use
.BR @accent ,
which the agent takes from the desktop's accent color (the portal's
.BR accent\-color ,
else KDE's
.BR AccentColor ,
else #3584e4).
Layers slide in 200\ ms.
.TP
.B light
Dark text on light keys, also with
.BR @accent .
The Touch Bar is an OLED panel, so lit pixels cost power: this theme draws more than the dark ones.
Layers slide in 200\ ms.
.TP
.B high\-contrast
White outlines and larger bold text on black.
A pressed key inverts, and a toggle that is on is solid yellow, so no state depends on hue alone.
Black costs as little power as the default.
Layers fade in 120\ ms.
.TP
.B classic
tiny\-dfr's look: gray buttons (0.2, and 0.4 when pressed), radius 8, 16\-pixel gaps, 32\-pixel bold
labels, no layer transition.
The tiny\-dfr importer picks it.
.PP
Every theme gets the desktop's
.BR @accent .
An unknown name is reported and
.B sliver
is used.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
@import "sliver:classic";
@define\-color accent #3584e4;

module            { border\-radius: 10px; padding: 0 18px; }
module:active     { background: @accent; }
#battery.critical { background: #c01c28; }
#custom\-vpn.connected { color: #33d17a; }
\&.zone\-main        { background: alpha(white, 0.06); border\-radius: 12px; }
bar.layer\-fn module { background: #1e1e24; }
module            { transition: background\-color 150ms ease\-out, width 200ms; }
bar               { \-sliver\-layer\-transition: fade 150ms; }
#taskbar          { \-sliver\-icon\-fit: content; }
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sliver\-config (5),
.BR sliver\-agent (1),
.BR sliver\-settings (1),
.BR waybar\-styles (5)
